      "slug": "why-mature-red-blood-cells-have-no-nucleus",
      "title": "成熟红细胞为什么要把细胞核“丢掉”？",
      "core_facts": [
        {
          "claim": "成熟哺乳动物红细胞通常无核、呈双凹圆盘状并含有血红蛋白。",
          "status": "verified",
          "sources": ["NCBI MeSH — Erythrocytes", "ASH/PMC — Red cell membrane disorders: structure meets function"]
        },
        {
          "claim": "哺乳动物红细胞在终末分化阶段经历染色质凝缩与排核，形成无核网织红细胞并继续成熟。",
          "status": "verified",
          "sources": ["PMC — Formation of mammalian erythrocytes: chromatin condensation and enucleation", "PMC — Emerging concepts in mammalian erythrocytes"]
        },
        {
          "claim": "无核化与血红蛋白装载、双凹形态和可变形性等功能特征相联系，但其演化驱动力不宜简化为单一原因。",
          "status": "verified",
          "sources": ["PMC — Formation of mammalian erythrocytes: chromatin condensation and enucleation", "PMC — Cellular dynamics of mammalian red blood cell production in the erythroblastic island niche", "ASH/PMC — Red cell membrane disorders: structure meets function"]
        },
        {
          "claim": "成熟红细胞缺乏细胞核和多数膜性细胞器，因此不具备普通有核细胞的完整转录与常规自我维护能力。",
          "status": "verified",
          "sources": ["NCBI MeSH — Erythrocytes", "PMC — Emerging concepts in mammalian erythrocytes", "ASH/PMC — Red cell membrane disorders: structure meets function"]
